        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$30.55$ marks",
          "worked": "Reading each stem as the tens digit gives 20 marks with total $611$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{x}&=\\frac{611}{20}\\\\\\overline{x}&=30.55\\text{ marks}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many students obtained a mark higher than the mean mark?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "10 students",
          "worked": "The marks greater than $30.55$ are $32,36,38,38,39,40,41,42,43,46$. Therefore, 10 students scored higher than the mean.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the standard deviation of their marks, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$10.22$ marks",
          "worked": "Enter all 20 marks into the calculator's statistics mode. Use population standard deviation, dividing by $20$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i-30.55)^2&=2088.95\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2088.95}{20}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx10.22\\text{ marks}\\end{align*}$$",
